--- Measures and lays out text for a terminal.
---
--- `term.width` returns the number of columns that a string takes, with
--- East Asian wide characters and emoji counted as two columns, combining
--- marks as none, and ANSI escape sequences skipped. `term.wrap` and
--- `term.truncate` fit text to a width and keep its colors across line
--- breaks. `term.table` and `term.box` draw tables and boxes.
--- `term.spinner` and `term.progress` report progress. They redraw in
--- place on a terminal and write plain lines to a file or a pipe.
---
--- Styled text comes from any source of ANSI escape sequences, such as the
--- `color` package.
---
--- @package term
--- @version 0.1.0
--- @lus 2.0
--- @license 0BSD
--- @repository https://github.com/lus-lang/atmos-term

local M = {}

-- Character widths -------------------------------------------------------------

-- Pairs of first and last code points, sorted. These characters take no
-- column: combining marks, format characters, and variation selectors.
local ZERO = {
    0x0300, 0x036F, 0x0483, 0x0489, 0x0591, 0x05BD, 0x05BF, 0x05BF, 0x05C1, 0x05C2, 0x05C4, 0x05C5,
